 "turns": [
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Hi, how's everything with you?",
   "est_sec": 1.65,
   "gap_before": 0.35,
   "role": "greeting",
   "phrasing": "greet_19"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Pretty relaxed today.",
   "est_sec": 1.03,
   "gap_before": 0.68,
   "event": "greeting_answer",
   "phrasing": "greet_ans_22"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "What do the little painted marks on trees mean? Some are white, some are yellow.",
   "est_sec": 4.75,
   "gap_before": 0.58,
   "block": "hiking.dlg14",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "They're called blazes, or waymarks. Each colour usually marks a different trail, so you follow one colour from start to finish.",
   "est_sec": 6.61,
   "gap_before": 0.8,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "hiking.dlg14"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "And when there are two stacked on top of each other?",
   "est_sec": 3.51,
   "gap_before": 1.02,
   "block": "hiking.dlg14",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "That usually means a turn is coming. If the top mark is offset to one side, the trail turns that way.",
   "est_sec": 6.61,
   "gap_before": 0.6,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "hiking.dlg14"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Oh, clever. I always thought",
   "est_sec": 1.65,
   "gap_before": 0.95,
   "event": "distractor",
   "kind": "pause",
   "block": "hiking.dlg14"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "someone was just bored with a paint can.",
   "est_sec": 2.58,
   "gap_before": 1.75,
   "block": "hiking.dlg14",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Ha, no, volunteers maintain most of them. If you go a long way without seeing one, you've probably missed a turn, so head back to the last one.",
   "est_sec": 8.78,
   "gap_before": 0.7,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "hiking.dlg14"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Changing the subject, I've got chicken thighs, a bag of spinach and some rice. The kids are hungry and I'm tired.",
   "est_sec": 6.61,
   "gap_before": 0.88,
   "block": "cooking.ctx1",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "You could do a quick garlic chicken and rice bowl, or a creamy spinach chicken in one pan. Which sounds better tonight?",
   "est_sec": 6.92,
   "gap_before": 0.89,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "cooking.ctx1"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Please give me fourteen seconds and then repeat the question.",
   "est_sec": 3.2,
   "gap_before": 0.87,
   "event": "instruction",
   "kind": "think_time",
   "wait_sec": 14,
   "phrasing": "think_instruction_v2_23"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Oh, but then again",
   "est_sec": 1.34,
   "anchor": {
    "turn": 11,
    "offset": 8.08
   },
   "event": "distractor",
   "kind": "self_talk",
